  "narrative": [
    "\"The BS programs require a minimum of 145 units, plus college general-education requirements in humanities and social sciences.\"",
    "\"To graduate, students must maintain an overall GPA of at least 2.0, and the department requires at least a C- grade in each course required for the major. All courses required for the major must be taken for a letter grade. This includes all lower-division math and science courses as well as the technical electives (TE).\"",
    "Screened major: overall UC San Diego GPA of 2.0 or above and C- or above in all screening courses (first-years: MATH 20A-B-C-D, MATH 18, PHYS 2A, SE 101A; transfers: MATH 20A-B-C-D, MATH 18, PHYS 2A-B-C, SE 101A).",
    "\"SE 1, SE 3, and SE 9 must be taken by all students majoring in structural engineering. Transfer students who have successfully petitioned to use a course equivalent to SE 101A prior to entering UC San Diego may take an additional technical elective in place of SE 1.\"",
    "\"A course cannot be taken both as part of a focus sequence and as a TE.\"",
    "Course requirements are given in the department's curriculum table; GE slots in the table are college requirements and are omitted."
  ],
